    {
      "id": "claim_35cdce94d2b14972bd1e066feff77b5d",
      "statement": "The installer, `install.sh` at the top of a checkout and of a release, needs `systemctl`, `curl` and `git`; it installs the `rusty-mcp`, `rusty-cli` and `rusty` binaries it finds in `bin/` beside it (a release tarball) and otherwise builds them with `cargo install --force --locked` from the checkout, then installs the unit from `service/`, enables and restarts it, probes it over HTTP with a two-second limit per try and checks that the unit itself is active, and deletes a leftover `~/.local/bin/rusty-session`; it installs no desktop entry, extra unit or key snippet.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://install.sh#L1-L63",
